<div class="mb-12 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-gray-50 p-6" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-5 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Frequently asked questions</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">What is the difference between automation and an AI agent?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Automation follows steps that people defined in advance. An agent is given a goal and chooses its own steps and tools. Anthropic describes workflows as LLMs and tools orchestrated through predefined code paths, and agents as LLMs that dynamically direct their own processes.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">What is AI orchestration?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">It is the coordination layer that decides which step, tool or agent runs next, passes context between them and tracks what happened. It can coordinate fixed workflows, agents, or both.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">Do I need AI agents?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Not always. Microsoft’s guidance says to use the lowest level of complexity that reliably meets your requirements, and simple repeatable tasks are usually better served by plain automation or a single model call.</p></div>
    <div><p class="mb-2 text-[17px] font-medium text-[#111827]">What is agent washing?</p><p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">Gartner uses the term for rebranding existing assistants, chatbots or RPA as agents. Ask a vendor which steps the system decides on its own and which are fixed.</p></div>
  </div>
</div>

